  {
   "tag": "a",
   "text": "01\n1966 Corvette Convertible — Updates Coming Soon\nThis 1966 Corvette Convertible is entering the next phase of its restoration. More photos, progress updates, and project details will be added soon as the work continues.",
   "region": "main",
   "y": 660,
   "x": 23,
   "font": "Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif",
   "size": "10px",
   "weight": "400",
   "color": "rgb(0, 0, 238)",
   "lh": "normal",
   "ls": "normal",
   "tt": "none",
   "align": "start",
   "href": "https://www.fitzgeraldclassics.com/portfolio-collections/portfolio/1966-corvette-convertible-%E2%80%94-updates-coming-soon",
   "bg": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)",
   "radius": "0px",
   "border": "0px none rgb(0, 0, 238)",
   "pad": "0px",
   "w": 456,
   "h": 223
  },
  {
   "tag": "a",
   "text": "02\n1957 Nash Metropolitan — Restoration in Progress\nPurchased as a remarkably solid but unfinished 1957 Nash Metropolitan, this project is being completed with a simple philosophy: preserve the character of the car, correct what matters, and invest where the finished result will have the greatest impact. This living project follows the restoration from its as-acquired condition and mechanical foundation through body preparation, interior work, electrical sorting, paint, trim, final assembly and road testing.\nPaint milestone — October 2026: Following the four coats of white applied on October 10, the white sections were carefully masked and the prepared upper body and hood received their yellow color. The latest photo sequence follows the car from primer and final masking through freshly applied yellow paint to the reveal of its yellow-and-white finish. Reflections across the panels capture the gloss, while the two-tone layout brings the Metropolitan's distinctive curves back into focus.\nCurrent status: The yellow-and-white paint is now applied, marking a major step toward the finished car. The restoration continues with paint finishing as needed, glass, lights, trim and hood-ornament installation, upholstery, final assembly and road testing. The hood ornament has already been test-fitted for alignment, and the original bench-seat frame has been sandblasted, powder coated in satin black and reassembled, ready for upholstery.\nUpdated October 12, 2026. Preserving Americana, one car at a time.",
   "region": "main",
   "y": 660,
   "x": 492,
   "font": "Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif",
   "size": "10px",
   "weight": "400",
   "color": "rgb(0, 0, 238)",
   "lh": "normal",
   "ls": "normal",
   "tt": "none",
   "align": "start",
   "href": "https://www.fitzgeraldclassics.com/portfolio-collections/portfolio/1957-nash-metropolitan-restoration-in-progress",
   "bg": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)",
   "radius": "0px",
   "border": "0px none rgb(0, 0, 238)",
   "pad": "0px",
   "w": 456,
   "h": 964
  },
  {
   "tag": "a",
   "text": "03\n1963 Ford Galaxie 500 Convertible\nA complete visual journey from a tired blue survivor to a refined white-and-turquoise American classic. This Fitzgerald Classics restoration follows the Galaxie through body preparation, paint, interior reconstruction, detail work and final assembly—preserving the character of Ford’s full-size 1960s convertible while giving every surface the attention it deserved.",
   "region": "main",
   "y": 660,
   "x": 962,
   "font": "Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif",
   "size": "10px",
   "weight": "400",
